# WP-273: the site is in c.o, unchanged; its target V (val, in d.o)
# moves by 24 bytes: the patch stays (its key is an unchanged file's), and
# its W4' is rewritten with V's new :lo12: offset.
proves: an update that moves an erratum 843419 site's target keeps the site's patch and rewrites its W4' (the load through the patch reads val); every hop is an update, equivalent to the full link
source: spec/landed/incr/WP-271.md §4 (e843419_target_moves), WP-273
edit A: d.S
hops: -, A, -, A
link: a.o c.o d.o
compilers: gcc
targets: a64
not kiln: assembly (.S): kiln compiles C++ only; the shape is written in the assembly
not x64: erratum 843419 is AArch64's (`--fix-cortex-a53-843419` is refused on x86-64, cli rows); x86-64 has no islands, its updates call no re-plan
nolibc: yes
options: --fix-cortex-a53-843419
